  - path: "docs/decisions/dec-58-a-sent-flow-is-sent-by-the-core-and-marked.html"
    tier: T2
    action: added
    distills: "The epic's load-bearing decision, landed at W1 before the screen. A sent flow is sent by the core's own client, sharing the proxy's upstream TLS trust and capture cap, and not looped through the proxy port. It is the third member of DEC-38's closed provenance enum, named sent rather than replayed because a composed request replays nothing; it names its seed, and the link may dangle. The call answers only once a reply exists, and a transport failure lands no flow, because a flow asserts an exchange happened. The header rules and why they are rules. The doors add no exposure beyond the proxy DEC-55's reach already arms."
